  "assumptions": [
    "Synthetic contrast response only; not an observed, normal, reduced or uniquely interpreted gravity field.",
    "All sources and evaluation points share the explicitly declared local Cartesian metre frame, vertical-up axis and height datum; caller performs any upstream coordinate/datum conversion.",
    "gx and gy follow the caller local x/y axes, which need not be true east/north. g_down=-gz_up; 1 mGal=1e-5 m/s^2.",
    "Potential is negative for positive contrasts, zero at infinity; acceleration=-gradient(potential).",
    "Uniform spheres use exact interior/centre/exterior formulae; overlapping sources superpose as density contrasts. Point masses have no physical radius and require a caller-selected exclusion distance.",
    "Sensitivities vary only source mass or density with fixed positions/radii; no geometry derivatives, inversion, geological uniqueness or propagated uncertainty.",
    "Pinned CODATA G is treated as a constant; its measurement uncertainty is not propagated. No curvature, rotation, reference field, softening or clipping."
  ],
